# Rank 1915 / CVE-2024-1023: vert.x's CombinerExecutor held its task tail in a
# per-instance netty FastThreadLocal (GHSA-5667-3wch-7q7w). Every FastThreadLocal
# instance permanently claims a slot in netty's InternalThreadLocalMap index and
# sizes every FastThreadLocalThread's array accordingly; the slot is never
# reclaimed, so a class instantiated per pool or per connection converts ordinary
# churn into unbounded growth of every event-loop thread's map. The pool package
# builds a CombinerExecutor per ConnectionPool, and the HTTP client builds pools
# per connection, so each connection leaks another index across all threads
# (memory exhaustion; the advisory pairs it with CVE-2024-1300 in DoS errata).
# The recorded CWE-119/CWE-200 does not describe the mechanism -- there is no
# buffer and no disclosure, the axis is unbounded per-instance allocation.
#
# The fixed revision (dd6f6430, PR #5082; 665ceba3 is the identical change on the 4.4
# branch via PR #5080) makes the field static -- one FastThreadLocal for the
# class -- and threads the executor identity through the stored value so
# interleaved executors do not interfere. The remediation is present at <fix>
# (`private static final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail<?>> current`, line 46)
# and absent at <fix>^ (`private final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail> current`,
# line 36). The discriminating fact is one keyword: static.
#
# The corpus family hint (CWE-444 body framing, code.AmbiguousMessageBodyFraming
# / VYQL-INJ-249) does not apply: this commit fixes a resource leak, not message
# framing, and the framing binding is Java. Vocabulary considered for the
# leak: code.UnboundedAllocationReview (VYQL-DOS-041, CWE-400/770) is the right
# judgement -- a construction that grows a per-thread array without bound per
# instance -- and is what this spec pins; ThreadLocalScopeOverwriteWithoutCleanup
# is a lifecycle-overwrite race, not per-instance allocation; the
# resource.ResourceLeak taint family (OwnerFree/ResourceHandle) needs a
# release-ordering path, and there is none: no untrusted value flows, the
# attacker's cost is the act of opening connections.
#
# Measured blocker, same family as rank 1637's engine-gap entry: a Java field
# declaration lowers to a bare nir.Assign with no modifier fact anywhere. The
# `field_declaration` case (java.go ~line 172) reads only the declared type;
# nir.Assign has no token slot; classMemberContextTokens (lowering.go:1297)
# skips Assign, so the analysis.class.context node carries class name, bases
# and method tokens but nothing about fields. `vyql graph` on the two blocks
# below is byte-identical -- the static keyword is erased at extraction. A
# probe binding on the FastThreadLocal constructor (callee.path ==
# "FastThreadLocal<>") labels exactly one node in both revisions, the same
# line, so no binding can score the fixed revision below the parent. A text route is not
# a substitute: the vulnerable file itself declares `protected static final
# class InProgressTail`, so any "static appears near the field" heuristic
# reads the vulnerable form as patched. Judged not mechanical, as at 1637 --
# emitting the fact means a change to shared IR plus the shared lowering walk
# plus the frontend, feeding the 512-token-capped class context node that
# every class-scope presence binding reads scan-wide. ENGINE-GAPS.md entry
# extends the 1637 item to field modifiers.
#
# Measured on the real checkout (--cache off, bounded): the change-carrying
# pool subtree (14 files) reports 0 findings at both revisions; the wider
# net subtree (76 files) reports 4 VYQL-SEC-002 hardcoded-secret rows at
# both revisions, none in the pool package. The shape's reachable set is
# exactly one site -- the only `new FastThreadLocal` in src/main/java; the
# other three FastThreadLocal-named files extend FastThreadLocalThread.
# Precision is therefore available; only the fact is missing. Both
# blocks assert reject VYQL-DOS-041: when a field's static-ness becomes
# extractable, a per-instance FastThreadLocal binding must flip the
# non-static block to expect while the static block stays reject.

test "rank1915: the combiner executor holds its task tail in a per-instance FastThreadLocal"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/io/vertx/core/net/impl/pool/CombinerExecutor.java
  reject VYQL-DOS-041
  code
  ```
  package io.vertx.core.net.impl.pool;

  import io.netty.util.concurrent.FastThreadLocal;
  import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

  public class CombinerExecutor<S> implements Executor<S> {

    protected static final class InProgressTail {
      Task task;
    }

    private final AtomicInteger s = new AtomicInteger();

    private final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail> current = new FastThreadLocal<>();

    @Override
    public void submit(Action<S> action) {
      s.incrementAndGet();
      InProgressTail inProgress = current.get();
      if (inProgress == null) {
        inProgress = new InProgressTail();
        current.set(inProgress);
        current.remove();
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1915: the fixed revision makes the FastThreadLocal one per class"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/io/vertx/core/net/impl/pool/CombinerExecutor.java
  reject VYQL-DOS-041
  code
  ```
  package io.vertx.core.net.impl.pool;

  import io.netty.util.concurrent.FastThreadLocal;
  import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

  public class CombinerExecutor<S> implements Executor<S> {

    protected static final class InProgressTail<S> {
      final CombinerExecutor<S> combiner;
      Task task;

      public InProgressTail(CombinerExecutor<S> combiner, Task task) {
        this.combiner = combiner;
        this.task = task;
      }
    }

    private final AtomicInteger s = new AtomicInteger();

    private static final FastThreadLocal<InProgressTail<?>> current = new FastThreadLocal<>();

    @Override
    public void submit(Action<S> action) {
      s.incrementAndGet();
      InProgressTail<S> inProgress = (InProgressTail<S>) current.get();
      if (inProgress == null) {
        inProgress = new InProgressTail<>(this, null);
        current.set(inProgress);
        current.remove();
      }
    }
  }
  ```
